1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,593
Last reaction: chlorine substitutes hydrogen.

2
00:00:03,593 --> 00:00:05,729
In the dark, it is selective.

3
00:00:05,729 --> 00:00:13,723
Only the alpha hydrogens, on the carbons next to oxygen, are replaced, giving the alpha, alpha dichloro ether.

4
00:00:13,723 --> 00:00:20,898
In bright sunlight, every hydrogen goes: perchloro diethyl ether, with ten molecules of chlorine.

